<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Entity>
  <!--
    NEW TABLE — wbs:4.7 (CO-007, EF-03), TAD docs/architecture/city-derivation-architecture.md
    ADR-001. One row per UK postcode outward code present in the client's delivered file
    (docs/Import/Postcode Details.xlsx, sheet Postcodes), holding the Main Postal Town / City
    value (FR-220-FR-222).

    WHY A TABLE, NOT A rev_setting ROW LIKE PostcodeRegionMap: the source file measures at
    3,394 outward-code rows (verified directly — header row, 3,394 data rows, zero blanks,
    zero duplicate outward codes, max outward-code length 4, max city-name length 20). A JSON
    array of that size cannot fit rev_setting.rev_value's MaxLength=4000 (TAD S1).

    SHAPE — deliberately SIMPLER than the sibling postcode-lookup local-authority register
    (TAD S1, S3): no rev_resolutionstatus column and no new global option set (ADR-002 — the
    source file has no ambiguity, so a miss is the ABSENCE of a row, not a populated-but-flagged
    one), no rev_lastseeninsource column (ADR-003 — this register is seeded once and never
    refreshed; CO-007 prices no refresh mechanism).

    ALTERNATE KEY on rev_name (outward code) — the proven pattern
    (rev_grant.rev_applicationid, IMP-0044; also used by rev_roundstatisticsresult below).
    Built after this table exists; index build is asynchronous — await EntityKeyIndexStatus
    = Active before the seed script's first upsert or the intake flow's first lookup relies
    on it (C-TECH-053, TAD S12.1).

    NOT PERSONAL DATA (NFR-220): public geographic reference data (outward code -> city
    name), same tier as rev_setting and the sibling rev_localauthorityregister. No column
    here is entered in constraints/domain/special-category-register.yml — neither
    `columns:` nor `pending_adjudication:` — because neither column identifies a person.

    RETENTION: indefinite, by design (TAD S3) — same posture as rev_setting. No data
    subject, no retention clock.

    SEEDED BY: provisioning/dataverse/seed-city-settlement-register.ps1, a one-off
    provisioning script (TAD ADR-003) — NOT a Cloud Flow. Reads
    provisioning/dataverse/data/city-settlement-register.csv (converted once, offline, from
    the client's .xlsx — TAD S4).

    NO FORM/VIEW OMITTED THIS TIME (contrast with rev_roundstatisticsresult below, which
    ships with none): TAD S9 asks for a minimal AllCitySettlementRegisters view and a
    SubArea under the existing Operations group, so this register is reachable for
    troubleshooting a miss rather than shipping unreachable the way rev_grant once did. Both
    are added — see SavedQueries/AllCitySettlementRegisters.xml and FormXml/main/.
  -->
  <Name LocalizedName="City Settlement Register" OriginalName="City Settlement Register">rev_citysettlementregister</Name>
  <EntityInfo>
    <entity Name="rev_citysettlementregister">
      <LocalizedNames>
        <LocalizedName description="City Settlement Register" languagecode="1033" />
      </LocalizedNames>
      <LocalizedCollectionNames>
        <LocalizedCollectionName description="City Settlement Registers" languagecode="1033" />
      </LocalizedCollectionNames>
      <Descriptions>
        <Description description="One row per UK postcode outward code in the client's delivered postcode file, holding the Main Postal Town / City value. Seeded once by provisioning/dataverse/seed-city-settlement-register.ps1, read by the intake flow's Lookup_city_register step, never refreshed (wbs:4.7, CO-007, TAD ADR-003)." languagecode="1033" />
      </Descriptions>
      <attributes>
        <attribute PhysicalName="rev_name">
          <Type>nvarchar</Type>
          <Name>rev_name</Name>
          <LogicalName>rev_name</LogicalName>
          <RequiredLevel>ApplicationRequired</RequiredLevel>
          <MaxLength>4</MaxLength>
          <Format>text</Format>
          <IsAuditEnabled>1</IsAuditEnabled>
          <IsSecured>0</IsSecured>
          <displaynames>
            <displayname description="Outward Code" languagecode="1033" />
          </displaynames>
          <Descriptions>
            <Description description="The UK postcode outward code (e.g. SW1A, AB10), upper-cased, no space — computed the same way the intake flow's existing Compute_outward_code step already computes it, so the intake lookup never re-derives outward-code logic a second way (TAD S3). MaxLength=4 matches the measured maximum across all 3,394 source rows. Never secured: this is the table's primary name attribute and cannot carry IsSecured=1 (C-TECH-070 clause 1, IMP-0249); nothing here needs securing regardless — a postcode outward code is not personal data on its own (NFR-220)." languagecode="1033" />
          </Descriptions>
        </attribute>
        <attribute PhysicalName="rev_cityname">
          <Type>nvarchar</Type>
          <Name>rev_cityname</Name>
          <LogicalName>rev_cityname</LogicalName>
          <RequiredLevel>ApplicationRequired</RequiredLevel>
          <MaxLength>100</MaxLength>
          <Format>text</Format>
          <IsAuditEnabled>1</IsAuditEnabled>
          <IsSecured>0</IsSecured>
          <displaynames>
            <displayname description="City Name" languagecode="1033" />
          </displaynames>
          <Descriptions>
            <Description description="The client file's Main Postal Town / City value for this outward code. Always populated for every row that exists (source measured with zero blank city values) — a miss is the absence of a row, not a populated-but-empty one (ADR-002). MaxLength=100 matches rev_applicant.rev_towncity's column width rather than the measured minimum (20 characters), so a future longer settlement name is not a schema change." languagecode="1033" />
          </Descriptions>
        </attribute>
      </attributes>
    </entity>
  </EntityInfo>
  <!-- A-CSR-01 (C-TECH-052): EntitySetName is a GUESS, not ground truth — Dataverse assigns
       the entity set name. Cheapest verification, per the same pattern rev_roundstatisticsresult
       used: EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='rev_citysettlementregister')?$select=EntitySetName
       after the first DEV prerequisite run. Do not hand-author it once the platform's answer
       is known — replace this guess with the read-back value. -->
  <EntitySetName>rev_citysettlementregisters</EntitySetName>
  <IsAuditEnabled>1</IsAuditEnabled>
  <IsRetrieveAuditEnabled>0</IsRetrieveAuditEnabled>
  <OwnershipType>OrganizationOwned</OwnershipType>
  <PrimaryNameAttribute>rev_name</PrimaryNameAttribute>
  <IsActivity>0</IsActivity>
  <HasNotes>0</HasNotes>
  <HasActivities>0</HasActivities>
  <EntityKeys>
    <EntityKey>
      <Name>rev_citysettlementregister_name</Name>
      <IsCustomizable>1</IsCustomizable>
      <displaynames>
        <displayname description="City Settlement Register Outward Code" languagecode="1033" />
      </displaynames>
      <EntityKeyAttributes>
        <AttributeName>rev_name</AttributeName>
      </EntityKeyAttributes>
    </EntityKey>
  </EntityKeys>
  <!-- D-018 FIX — see Entities/rev_applicant/Entity.xml for the full rationale. Without
       these two elements this entity's SavedQueries file and its FormXml/main file pack
       silently to zero, exactly as rev_errorlog's own identical comment warns — both are
       populated for this entity (TAD S9), unlike rev_roundstatisticsresult's deliberately
       empty pair. -->
  <FormXml />
  <SavedQueries />
</Entity>
